// v160: c133 — ACCESSIBILITY + I18N SWEEP (portal): every icon-only control now has a localized accessible name — the header buttons (font −/+, theme, theme menu, settings), water +/−, rest timer −15/+30/✕, viewer close and the diary ✕ are labelled through 11 new a11y keys ×3 languages (the static HTML had English-only aria/title attributes); workout set rows got real semantics: the ✓ done toggle announces aria-pressed + «Отметить подход выполненным», the type-cycler title/aria shows the CURRENT set type (incl. the previously key-less 'normal' → setNormal), RPE chips carry aria-pressed per value, and the previously untranslated title="type"/"Superset"/"min ⇄ sec" now follow the language (supersetLabel / timeToggle); the report and unlock overlays are proper role="dialog" aria-modal=true with names (reportTitle/unlockTitle), the report remembers its opener and restores focus on close, and ESCAPE now closes the report too (same tolerant path as viewer/exercise — the session is untouched, «Завершить» reopens it); the analytics SVGs accept opts.ariaLabel (sparkBars → aTrendT, progressLines → aProgressT) so the charts are announced instead of role=img-without-name; the activity calendar is forced direction:ltr so the МЕСЯЦ/6-week timeline stays chronological in RTL (the charts precedent); the recovery sparkline gains direction:ltr; renderARecent's stray «·reps» under a kg/lb tonnage got replaced with the localized «N/M подходов»; settings sheet: shade palette group + close button labelled. Engine: analytics-engine version c133 + ariaLabel support (trainer call sites unchanged, attribute added only when the app passes a label); recovery-engine sparkSVG direction:ltr. Verified: scripts/test-c133.cjs; browser harness at 412px RU/EN/HE (aria labels live-switch, aria-pressed on RPE, report dialog name + focus + Escape, calendar ltr). Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c133, cache dk-gym-v160
