// v162: c135 — VOICE COACH (spoken guidance for blind trainees, portal): NEW shared module src/voice-coach.js (window.dkVoiceCoach, same load pattern as the engines) — device TTS only (speechSynthesis, ru/en/he, works offline, zero assets); queue with priorities (nav/alert interrupt, info/step queue), rapid-repeat dedupe for toasts only (nav repeats and «Повторить» step ALWAYS speak), sentence-aware chunking ≤180 chars (mobile engines drop long utterances), a per-utterance WATCHDOG (iOS sometimes never fires onend and killed the queue silently), local-voice-first pick with per-language list, graceful no-voice return, emoji/symbol stripping before speech. PORTAL: settings sheet gains «🎧 Голосовой тренер» (main toggle, Обзорный/Подробный level, speed 70–130%, voice picker for the current language with honest «no voice installed» warning, test-voice button) — global device prefs dk_voice_on/_level/_rate/_name, and dk_voice_optout so the trainee's own OFF always beats the trainer preset; the narrator announces section tabs and day tabs, repeats every toast (saves/errors/rest-done), and reads the TECHNIQUE step-by-step: a 🔊 button on every exercise card in the workout list + a player in the exercise modal (▶ Прочитать технику / ⏭ Далее / 🔁 Повторить / ⏹ Стоп + «Шаг N / M» + haptics per step), FULL level auto-starts the reader when the exercise modal opens, closing the modal stops the narration. TRAINER: portal-link modal gains «Для незрячего клиента (голосовой диктор)» — stored as client.portal_blind, regenerates the link, payload carries blind_voice:true → the portal auto-enables the narrator in FULL mode on that device unless the client opted out. Module unit-tested end-to-end with a stubbed engine (scripts/test-voice-coach.cjs 38/38: chunking/cleaning/voice pick/queue/interrupt/dedupe/step lifecycle/watchdog/stopAll). Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c135, cache dk-gym-v162
// v163: c136 — VOICE WORKOUT MODE (portal): the narrator now guides the WHOLE live workout, not just technique. Events (level-aware: Brief = the meaningful ones, Full = everything): workout start «Тренировка начата. День A. Упражнения: 6» / resume «Продолжаем тренировку» (startOrResumeDay knows fresh vs resumed), every ✓ set «Подход 2 выполнен» + at FULL level the next-set hint «Следующий подход: 70 килограммов, повторов 8» (exercise's own unit word), un-✓ «отменён», rest timer start «Отдых 90 секунд» (toasts already cover rest-done/save/errors), add/remove set and the type cycler announce themselves at FULL, and the finish summary «Тренировка завершена. Подходы: 12 из 15. Объём: 3200 килограммов» (display unit — lb spoke as «фунтов»). All phrases are proper spoken words (not «кг»/«×») composed from new i18n keys ×3. WAKE LOCK: while the narrator is on and a session is active the screen is kept awake (navigator.wakeLock, re-acquired on visibilitychange, released at finish) — the phone no longer sleeps mid-set. BIGGER TARGETS: body.voice-mode bumps ✓/RPE/inputs/set-row sizes for gloved gym fingers (pure CSS, toggled by voiceApply). The exercise modal now lands focus on its close button and returns it to the opener on close (report modal precedent). i18n: voiceStart/voiceResume/voiceSetWord/voiceSetDone/voiceSetUndone/voiceNextSet/voiceKg/voiceLb/voiceReps/voiceRest/voiceRestSec/voiceFinish/voiceSetAdded/voiceSetRemoved × ru/en/he. Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c136, cache dk-gym-v163
// v164: c137 — TECHNIQUE PLAYER FIXES + «НАЧАТЬ ТРЕНИРОВКУ» (portal, real-device feedback from the coach): the reader used to speak step 1 and go silent — steps now AUTO-CONTINUE with an 800ms breathing gap (module opts.auto default true + opts.gapMs; every step is its own utterance, the next starts when the previous ends); «Стоп» used to WIPE the selection — stopSteps is now PAUSE (keeps the position, cancels the pending auto-timer) while resetSteps clears, so «▶» RESUMES from the current step (portal tracks WHICH exercise the player holds via key — a finished run restarts from 1, a paused one continues), the counter keeps the last position at the end, and tapping any step in the modal technique list jumps the playback there (buttons + stepGoto/startIndex, active step highlighted & gently scrolled into view). The pause guard matters: cancel() fires onend, so the onend handler checks _paused before the auto-advance or a pause would have stepped forward. «Начать тренировку» — the portal's main CTA renamed from «В зал» in ru/en/he + startHint texts (lock banner & finish-flow hint included) — clearer for every trainee, crucial for the blind audience. Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c137, cache dk-gym-v164
// v165: c138 — THE NARRATOR SPEAKS EVERYTHING (portal, FULL level): a generic tap-reader now announces the accessible name of EVERY button/tab/link the trainee touches (aria-label → title → visible text, controls can carry data-voice-hint for a friendlier phrase; a 500ms timestamp guard stops double speech when a specific handler already spoke: sets, RPE, day tabs, finish…), selects announce the chosen option, and FOCUSED fields introduce themselves: weight «Вес, килограммы» (the exercise's own unit), reps «Повторения», time/dist labels, check-in weight/waist/hip, diary fields — with the current value when present. ENTERED VALUES are spoken back: «12 килограммов» / «20 фунтов» (unit-aware), «8 повторов», time as minutes/seconds per the exercise's tunit, distance as meters/kilometers via the exposed dkCUnitGetPortal; committed on change + a 900ms debounced read while typing; the private check-in note is never read. RPE («шкала 1–10»): tapping a chip says «Уровень тяжести 8 из 10», clearing says «Уровень тяжести отменён». UNIT SWITCHES are spoken: the kg/lb chip carries a data-voice-hint with the CURRENT unit and the sheet selection says «Килограммы»/«Фунты» (per-exercise sheet too), cardio units say «Минуты/Секунды/Метры/Километры». New i18n × ru/en/he: voiceRpe/voiceMinutes/voiceMeters/voiceKm/voiceCm/voiceUnitKg/voiceUnitLb. Everything is FULL-level only (Brief keeps the meaningful-event mix). Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c138, cache dk-gym-v165
// v166: c139 — PORTAL TOUCH FIXES (real-device feedback): the exercise modal could NOT be scrolled — #exercise-view sat in a flex column without flex-1/min-h-0, so its content overflowed the max-h-[92vh] container and was clipped by overflow-hidden («10 шагов техники — видно три с половиной»); it is now a proper scroll pane (flex-1 min-h-0 overscroll-contain) and every step stays reachable. And the exercise card no longer opens from ANY tap on its body (a stray miss at a blind trainee exploded a modal): the title/paragraphs/rows are inert, the card opens ONLY from the thumbnail or the new 👁 button beside the title (localized a11yOpenCard ×3) — the opener is still remembered for focus restore. Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c139, cache dk-gym-v166
// v167: c140 — SUPERSET GROUPS (link model, real-device feedback «два суперсета считаются одним четверным»): supersets are LINKS now — ss_link:true on exercise i means «i and i+1 form a superset»; a group is a consecutive LINK CHAIN, so A-B + C-D stay TWO pairs instead of one quadruple, triples/quads/quintuples build naturally (each ⚡ tap links THIS exercise with the NEXT: not-in-group → link (chains merge when the next already leads one), linked-to-next → split after this exercise, linked-to-prev → the pair turns off from that side, last-without-next → honest hint). Legacy data (is_superset flag runs) migrates to links on the first pass; is_superset/superset_partner remain normalized for older consumers. EVERY group gets its OWN COLOR from a 6-color palette (order = group order) drawn as an inline border/background/glow style in the program builder, the trainer's live workout and the client portal (was: one amber frame for everything). ✓/Сделал всё/add/remove set sync now spans the whole CHAIN in both apps; reorder/auto-arrange/cross-day moves still clear links (stale pairing); the live→program save compare includes ss_link. ss_link travels through every mapping (builder → saved program, template, live session, save-back both ways, portal share → session). Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c140, cache dk-gym-v167
// v168: c141 — LIVE WORKOUT CLEANUP + EXERCISE REORDER (trainer, real-device feedback: «строка с выбором клиентов ничего не меняет… кнопка Килограмм тоже»): the client selector and the global kg/lb chip are REMOVED from the live workout screen — inside a session the client is already fixed (server: nothing to switch mid-workout) and the weight unit is a per-exercise concern (every exercise card carries its own unit chip); the dead wiring (clientSel change handler, loadClientList guard already tolerates the missing select) and the stale #lw-unit-chip CSS went with them. NEW: every live exercise card gets ↑/↓ buttons next to the view/⚡/✕ cluster — a freshly added exercise lands at the bottom and can be moved up on the spot; the move uses the program builder's exact reorder rule (a move invalidates «this + next» superset links, so links are cleared for the day), marks the session as structurally changed (the finish flow offers to save the new order into the program — the existing ids/order comparison picks it up) and is fully disabled at the list edges. workouts.moveUp/moveDown/moved × ru/en/he. Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c141, cache dk-gym-v168
// v169: c142 — CHIP ROWS THAT ALWAYS FIT + UNIT-TRUE PLACEHOLDER (real-device feedback): the portal's program / day / plan chip rows used overflow-x-auto with a hidden scrollbar — on desktop a mouse cannot drag them and the 4th program stayed a «little tuft» off-screen. They now FLEX-WRAP: every program (and every day, every plan) is always fully visible and tappable, no hidden content at any font scale. In the trainer's program editor the per-set weight input showed a hardcoded «кг» placeholder even when the exercise's unit was pounds (the «фт» chip above was right, the box below lied) — the placeholder now carries the exercise's REAL unit short (кг/фт). Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c142, cache dk-gym-v169
// v170: c143 — CARDIO FIELDS PER MACHINE (real-device feedback): «Усилие» is meaningless on machines — a treadmill has SPEED and an INCLINE (подъём 1–20), bikes/ellipticals/steppers/rowers have a RESISTANCE LEVEL (1–20). dkCardioMachine() detects the machine from the exercise's names + equipment in RU/EN/HE (treadmill/бегов/дорожк/הליכון → speed+incline; bike/вело/эргометр/אופני, ellip/эллипс/אליפטי, stepper/степпер, rowing/греб, skierg/лыж → level; any other cardio → level). The PROGRAM BUILDER replaces the effort input with the machine's fields for cardio rows; the trainer LIVE WORKOUT renders them as a second line under time/distance; the CLIENT PORTAL renders the same line (speed+incline or level, localized ×3) and its input handler + finish-record mapping carry speed/incline/level through. Prescribed machine values survive program → live; all 8 set-mapping points keep the new fields (trainer live build/save, template copies, portal finish, trainer→portal history). New i18n workouts.speed/incline/level (trainer JSONs) + speedLabel/inclineLabel/levelLabel (portal islands) ×3. Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c143, cache dk-gym-v170
// v171: c144 — SET TIMER + SOUND THAT MATTERS (portal + trainer live): every TIME-BASED set (cardio, warm-ups, stretching, handstands/planks…) gets a ▶ interval timer inside the row — it counts the set's OWN time (tunit-aware: sec stays sec, min ×60), shows mm:ss right on the button (▶ again = cancel), and at zero rings the LOUD bell and announces «Время вышло» (voice coach). The completion bell is TWICE AS LOUD as the old rest beep (portal 0.18→0.36, trainer 0.3→0.6) — exactly what was asked. And PROGRESS IS HEARD: a ✓ on a set that beats last time (weight×reps vs prev_weight×prev_reps; bodyweight compares reps only) plays a pleasant rising three-tone chime + «Прогресс — лучше прошлого раза» for the narrator — in BOTH apps (portal done handler + trainer live ✓ handler via shared dkLiveProgressCheck). Timers stop themselves on finish/save (no orphans after "Сохранить"). New i18n ×3: portal a11ySetTimer/voiceTimerStart/voiceTimeUp/voiceProgress/timerNoTime; trainer workouts.setTimer/timeUp/progress/noTime. Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c144, cache dk-gym-v171
// v172: c145 — HONEST VOICES (real-device feedback: Windows has only RU engines, Android only EN → Russian/Hebrew produced «странные звуки»): the voice core gained STRICT mode — if no voice exists for the active language, the phrase is NOT spoken at all (an English engine reading Hebrew is exactly the gibberish that was heard); speak() and speakSteps() both refuse and report through onMissingVoice. The portal: a one-time spoken notice in an AVAILABLE language of the trio («Голос для выбранного языка не установлен…» ru/en/he), a persistent 🎙️ amber badge in the hero that opens the settings diagnostics, and a diagnostics block in the voice settings: RU/EN/HE status (✓ N голосов / ✗ не установлен) refreshed on voiceschanged + «Обновить», a per-language «Проверить», and a per-platform install guide (Windows / Android / iPhone+iPad / macOS, auto-detected by UA, copyable) — Windows speech packs or Edge online voices, Google TTS «Установить голосовые данные», iOS Spoken Content → Voices. The chosen voice is remembered PER LANGUAGE (dk_voice_name_ru/_en/_he; the legacy dk_voice_name migrates into the current language once) so «Автоматически по языку» finally means what it says; enabling the narrator without a voice opens the guide instead of playing a garbled test phrase. Module unit tests strict behavior; static + browser harness verify silence/notice/badge/diagnostics/live recovery after a voice appears. Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c145, cache dk-gym-v172
// v173: c146 — NUTRITION BUG SWEEP (audit P0/P1): the daily log was UN-FINDABLE in UTC+2/+3 — records stored local midnight but were looked up through toISOString (UTC), so yesterday's food «disappeared» and empty duplicates piled up (now dkLogDateKey + local-midnight construction everywhere, the date input defaults to LOCAL today); the portal used to read f.name / meal.name while plans store name_ru/en/he + nutrition and labelKey/customLabel (every product «?», every meal «Приём» — now mealLabelOf/foodNameOf/foodCalOf with meal-label i18n ×3); the daily-log local search read the EMPTY food_base store while 2344 reference products live in food_database (now searches BOTH, normalizes reference items, shows localized names, cap 60); calcMacros computed fat/carbs from the FULL calorie target ignoring the protein calories (plans overshot — now split the remaining, renormalized, protein capped at 45%, calorie band 800–6000 in calcMacros + calcTargetCalories); computeAdherence read actual_* fields nothing wrote (permanent «—» — now derived from meals[].items[] portion totals). P1: food-detail save preserves name_ru/serving_quantity/package_grams/is_archived (Object.assign over the existing record) + a Russian-name field in the editor; search by brand/barcode/category in the picker AND the DB browser; picker starts from the product's real serving_quantity/package_grams instead of always 100 г; adjustMacro/scaleAllPortions keep unit_amount truthful; plan targets validated+clamped; the literal ${t(...)} template strings in the static HTML fixed; the hidden «Add food» button restored; double wiring of np-close/np-save/fp-close/fp-search guarded (every save fired twice). Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c146, cache dk-gym-v173
// v174: c147 — FOOD IMAGES, BUNDLED (user choice «все в репозиторий»): all 2180 product photos from food-db.json are now downloaded ONCE and shipped inside the app — food-images/<id>.jpg, resized to ≤256 px JPEG q80, 19.7 MB total (the initial run took ~45 s, zero failures; scripts/fetch-food-images.cjs is resume-safe and re-runnable). A new helper (window.dkFoodImgTag in the trainer, foodImgTag in the portal) renders the LOCAL file first, the external URL as the second chance (onerror chain) and a 🥗 placeholder behind it when both fail — so photos work OFFLINE and no longer depend on openfoodfacts/foodsd hotlinks. The PORTAL finally SHOWS photos: workout-day meal plan rows and the diary search results got 36px thumbnails; the trainer's picker + database browser rows grew to 36px with the same local-first chain, and the food-detail card uses it too. SW: the existing stale-while-revalidate static branch caches /food-images/ automatically (offline after first view; APP_SHELL untouched — no 20 MB precache). copy-assets ships the folder to dist. Verification: data audit (2180/2180 files, JPEG magic bytes, 1.2–120 KB each, failures.json empty), static wiring tests, portal harness on the built dist (meal thumb naturalWidth>0, diary search thumb naturalWidth>0). Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c147, cache dk-gym-v174
// v175: c148 — NUTRITION BRIDGE (client → coach): the portal now CLOSES THE LOOP on food. Every plan item got a real «съел» checkbox (state per day+plan in dk_nutr_<date>, a plan switch resets stale marks), the nutrition tab gained four SVG rings «съедено/цель» (kcal/P/F/C; red when >105% of target) and a MICRONUTRIENTS card (fiber/sodium/iron/calcium/potassium/vit C, % of RDI, counted from the checked items' real nutrition from the 2344-product DB). New dkNutrSnapshot() (date/ts/plan/target/totals/items≤40/diary≤30) is mirrored into the SAME shared cloud doc as the workout history — additive `nutr` field, merged by date, cap 90 days — and ALL doc writers (portal dkHistPushRaw/dkPushChecks + trainer dkPushClientHistory/dkSyncClientHistory) preserve it, so no side can erase the other. Pushes are debounced (1.5 s) on every checkbox/diary change and fire on boot/online/flush. TRAINER: the analytics screen fetches the days next to the body check-ins (5 s race, stale-client guarded), shows a «Питание из портала» card (7-day fact/plan bars, color-coded, latest day with food names) and MERGES the portal days into computeAdherence — one log per date, the portal day wins over the trainer's plan log (nutrToLogs + dkMergeNutrition), so the adherence metric finally reflects what the client actually ate. New i18n ×3: portal nutrProgressTitle/nutrMicroTitle/nutrMicroHint + 6 nutrient labels; trainer analytics.nutrTitle/nutrHint/nutrAvg/nutrLast. Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c148, cache dk-gym-v175
// v176: c149 — THE GENERATOR COMES BACK (Phase-4 surgery had deleted the HTML while the JS stayed): the `#generator-modal` skeleton is restored (header + #generator-subtitle + #generator-close, #generator-loading, #generator-results with profile-summary/rules/split, the footer with Regenerate/Start) so BOTH dead flows work again — the rule-based WORKOUT program generator (questionnaire: split/session-time/duration/focus/injuries/source) and the NUTRITION meal-plan generator (goal/activity/diet/meals/calories). The nutrition footer was ALSO missing its primary button — the wiring for #nutrition-generate existed but the button did not (only Cancel + AI Pro were rendered) — restored as Cancel | Generate | AI Pro. NEW questionnaire fields (c149): SEX (feeds the BMR Mifflin-St Jeor sign), ALLERGIES (6 chips → the food filter's keyword map) and LIKED/DISLIKED foods — prefilled from the client card, persisted back to it on Generate (applyProfileOverrides) and passed as a merged client to both rule-based and AI generation. The client card got its missing Nutrition Profile section back (sex + allergies + cuisine/budget/cook-time/target weight/goal weeks/stress/sleep/work hours/liked/disliked — the JS had been reading these fields with guards for years) and the AI Configuration settings panel is restored (endpoint/key/model + Save/Test/Clear + live status) so AI Pro is configurable with a user key again. New i18n client.sex/sexHint ×3 (everything else reused existing keys). Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c149, cache dk-gym-v176
// v177: c150 — SMART FOOD SEARCH (trainer + portal): the food picker finally REMEMBERS. FAVORITES (⭐ toggle on every result card, trainer-wide dk_food_favs) and RECENT (dk_food_recent, auto-filled when a food is added to a meal) appear as filter chips (All/Favorites/Recent/Recipes) and as the opening view of the search modal — no more retyping the same product every day. PORTIONS FROM THE PRODUCT: the reference items now carry serving_quantity/package_grams through the normalizer, the portion modal opens on the product's REAL serving (not always 100 g) and shows quick-portion chips (100 g / Serving · X g / Package · Y g); the portal diary does the same (grams auto-set + unit chips under the entry fields). RECIPES (trainer): a new recipe builder — name + product search dropdown + ingredient rows with editable grams, live totals + per-100 g recalculation (recipeTotals, pure), saved into food_base as source:'recipe' with the ingredient list and one-serving size = total weight, instantly searchable/pickable like any product. Portal search results got the ⭐ toggle + recent/favorites opening view (namespaced per client). New i18n ×3 (trainer food.filter*/fav*/recent*/no*/portion*/recipe*; portal diaryFav*/diaryRecentTitle/diaryPortion*). Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c150, cache dk-gym-v177
// v178: c151 — THE PORTAL BECOMES AN APP (foundation): (1) SECURITY — Firestore rules for /portal_shares are now GET-ONLY: `list` was open, so anyone holding the config could enumerate every encrypted share AND the plaintext history docs (workouts, weight/waist/hip check-ins, nutrition) and even DELETE them (`allow delete: if true`); now list and delete are denied, writes keep the size guard. The trainer's Settings → Cloud copyable rules text was updated (one-time republish needed). (2) THE PORTAL REGISTERS THE SERVICE WORKER ITSELF — before only the trainer app did, so a client who installed the portal directly had no offline cache and no PWA install path. (3) REMEMBER ME — after a successful unlock the share + access code are remembered: the next launch shows «С возвращением! Продолжить как <имя>?» — ONE TAP, no code (the «продолжить с того же места» request); «Ввести код заново» stays one tap away. (4) LOCK / LOGOUT — explicit «🔒 Заблокировать» and «Выйти» (confirm; erases the session + device data and lands on a proper «Портал не подключён» screen instead of demo data), auto-lock after a long background stay (selectable 5/10/30/off, pure dkLockDue check), and the fresh-link flow now falls back to the cached blob on ANY fetch error (not only offline). (5) NO ACCIDENTAL EXIT — browser-back during an active workout asks first, beforeunload guards a live session; installed PWA has no back at all. (6) PWA POLISH — install banner (native prompt on Android/desktop, Share → Add to Home Screen hint on iOS, dismissible for 30 days), navigator.storage.persist() so the browser stops evicting the portal data. (7) SW INSTALL SURVIVES ONE BAD FILE — cache.addAll was all-or-nothing, so one flaky/oversized entry (the 21 MB exercise-db.json) could kill the ENTIRE precache and leave the app with no service worker; install now caches each URL best-effort. New portal i18n ×3 (continue/lock/logout/app/install/autolock/exit strings). Versions: meta/footer/RUNNING c151, cache dk-gym-v